      "source_sha256": "475626d949cf9fac967ccd5b879f150cf520ca1ad0c74fbd0324028e2577c140",
      "text": "(SUPERVISE A0 (PARALLEL (PAIR B1 C1) (PAIR B2 C2)))"
    },
    {
      "byte_end": 960,
      "byte_start": 851,
      "char_end": 949,
      "char_start": 840,
      "document": "S25",
      "id": "anchor:S25:840-949",
      "sort": "SourceAnchor",
      "source_sha256": "475626d949cf9fac967ccd5b879f150cf520ca1ad0c74fbd0324028e2577c140",
      "text": "A0 is a NEW supervisor fork from original A with a snapshot of its context, but pending calls NOT duplicated."
    },
    {
      "byte_end": 1121,
      "byte_start": 961,
      "char_end": 1110,
      "char_start": 950,
      "document": "S25",
      "id": "anchor:S25:950-1110",
      "sort": "SourceAnchor",
      "source_sha256": "475626d949cf9fac967ccd5b879f150cf520ca1ad0c74fbd0324028e2577c140",
      "text": "B1 and C1 are role aliases for the ORIGINAL A and B, preserving their exact stable agent identities, private state, pipe cursor and ongoing turn during wrapping"
    },
    {
      "byte_end": 1257,
      "byte_start": 1204,
      "char_end": 1246,
      "char_start": 1193,
      "document": "S25",
      "id": "anchor:S25:1193-1246",
      "sort": "SourceAnchor",
      "source_sha256": "475626d949cf9fac967ccd5b879f150cf520ca1ad0c74fbd0324028e2577c140",
      "text": "B2 and C2 are NEW logical agents with new identities."
    },
    {
      "byte_end": 1541,
      "byte_start": 1258,
      "char_end": 1530,
      "char_start": 1247,
      "document": "S25",
      "id": "anchor:S25:1247-1530",
      "sort": "SourceAnchor",
      "source_sha256": "475626d949cf9fac967ccd5b879f150cf520ca1ad0c74fbd0324028e2577c140",
      "text": "PAIR1 and PAIR2 are independently-running child REGIONS with their own loop instance, private role-specific mailboxes, flow-local in/out buffers, pipes, independent subscriber cursors, correlation/activation/iteration identities, retained messages/effects/receipts and restart state."
    },
    {
      "byte_end": 1847,
      "byte_start": 1710,
      "char_end": 1834,
      "char_start": 1699,
      "document": "S25",
      "id": "anchor:S25:1699-1834",
      "sort": "SourceAnchor",
      "source_sha256": "475626d949cf9fac967ccd5b879f150cf520ca1ad0c74fbd0324028e2577c140",
      "text": "parent may observe child events/results and request parent-exit but must NOT enter child's private mailboxes or gate each B↔C exchange."
    },
    {
      "byte_end": 1953,
      "byte_start": 1848,
      "char_end": 1940,
      "char_start": 1835,
      "document": "S25",
      "id": "anchor:S25:1835-1940",
      "sort": "SourceAnchor",
      "source_sha256": "475626d949cf9fac967ccd5b879f150cf520ca1ad0c74fbd0324028e2577c140",
      "text": "Each child can produce local exit; parent exit must be addressed, correlated and exercised at a boundary."
    },
    {
      "byte_end": 2100,
      "byte_start": 1954,
      "char_end": 2081,
      "char_start": 1941,
      "document": "S25",
      "id": "anchor:S25:1941-2081",
      "sort": "SourceAnchor",
      "source_sha256": "475626d949cf9fac967ccd5b879f150cf520ca1ad0c74fbd0324028e2577c140",
      "text": "Finite budget/cancellation semantics: ENTER→RUNNING→EXIT_REQUESTED→EXITED or equivalent, no unbounded loop; no autonomous background runner."
    },
    {
      "byte_end": 2233,
      "byte_start": 2101,
      "char_end": 2214,
      "char_start": 2082,
      "document": "S25",
      "id": "anchor:S25:2082-2214",
      "sort": "SourceAnchor",
      "source_sha256": "475626d949cf9fac967ccd5b879f150cf520ca1ad0c74fbd0324028e2577c140",
      "text": "Actual independent interleaving: both pairs can advance independently and in either order, progress of one must not block the other."
    },
    {
      "byte_end": 2328,
      "byte_start": 2234,
      "char_end": 2309,
      "char_start": 2215,
      "document": "S25",
      "id": "anchor:S25:2215-2309",
      "sort": "SourceAnchor",
      "source_sha256": "475626d949cf9fac967ccd5b879f150cf520ca1ad0c74fbd0324028e2577c140",
      "text": "Prove identity and current state preserved before/after wrapping, no messages lost/duplicated."
    },
    {
      "byte_end": 2465,
      "byte_start": 2329,
      "char_end": 2446,
      "char_start": 2310,
      "document": "S25",
      "id": "anchor:S25:2310-2446",
      "sort": "SourceAnchor",
      "source_sha256": "475626d949cf9fac967ccd5b879f150cf520ca1ad0c74fbd0324028e2577c140",
      "text": "Parent remains live and maintains child refs; restarts reconstruct every region, exports, mailboxes, pipes, states, cursors and history."
    },
    {
      "byte_end": 2632,
      "byte_start": 2466,
      "char_end": 2613,
      "char_start": 2447,
      "document": "S25",
      "id": "anchor:S25:2447-2613",
      "sort": "SourceAnchor",
      "source_sha256": "475626d949cf9fac967ccd5b879f150cf520ca1ad0c74fbd0324028e2577c140",
      "text": "Allow additive runtime growth: create B2/C2 and their flow-local mailboxes and wire them without deleting PAIR1 history; version/revision receipts and stable exports."
    },
    {
      "byte_end": 2681,
      "byte_start": 2633,
      "char_end": 2662,
      "char_start": 2614,
